.TH FORGEKIT-REMOVE 1 "2026-08-25" "ForgeKit 0.3.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
forgekit-remove \- Remove a feature from an existing ForgeKit project
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B forgekit remove
\fIfeature\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove a previously installed feature from a ForgeKit project. Before removal,
ForgeKit verifies that no other installed features depend on the feature
being removed and detects user modifications to feature files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-plan
Show the removal plan without making changes
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug output
.TP
.B \-\-format \fIformat\fR
Output format: human, json (default: human)
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Reduce output (except errors and JSON)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Preview auth feature removal:
.B forgekit remove auth --plan
.TP
Remove auth feature:
.B forgekit remove auth
.TP
Remove with JSON output:
.B forgekit remove auth --format json
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Feature not installed, dependency conflict, or user modifications detected
.TP
.B 2
Execution error
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./.forge/features.yaml
Installed features tracking (updated)
.TP
.I ./forge.yaml
Project configuration (may be updated)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR forgekit (1),
.BR forgekit-add (1)
.SH AUTHOR
ForgeKit Contributors <forgekit@demetrius-ch.github.io>